1
00:00:02,342 --> 00:00:04,469
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,719 --> 00:00:06,387
Earth.

3
00:00:06,721 --> 00:00:08,598
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,642
Air.

5
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:14,646
Long ago, the four nations lived
together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,313 --> 00:00:19,234
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,359 --> 00:00:23,780
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:23,905 --> 00:00:26,741
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

9
00:00:27,158 --> 00:00:30,828
100 years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

10
00:00:30,954 --> 00:00:32,705
an airbender named Aang.

11
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:35,124
And although his airbending
skills are great,

12
00:00:35,208 --> 00:00:37,794
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

13
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:38,920
AANG: Oof!

14
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:41,881
But I believe Aang can save the world.

15
00:01:10,872 --> 00:01:14,042
Spare coins for weary travelers?

16
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:15,377
( COINS CLINKING )

17
00:01:15,919 --> 00:01:17,963
This is humiliating. We're royalty.

18
00:01:18,088 --> 00:01:20,548
These people should be
giving us whatever we want.

19
00:01:20,674 --> 00:01:23,134
They will, if you ask nicely.

20
00:01:25,303 --> 00:01:29,599
Spare change for a hungry old man?

21
00:01:30,016 --> 00:01:31,977
Aw, here you go.

22
00:01:32,477 --> 00:01:38,358
The coin is appreciated,
but not as much as your smile.

23
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:39,985
( GIGGLES )

24
00:01:41,861 --> 00:01:44,864
How about some entertainment
in exchange for...

25
00:01:45,031 --> 00:01:46,616
A gold piece?

26
00:01:46,825 --> 00:01:48,785
We're not performers.

27
00:01:49,286 --> 00:01:51,162
Not professional, anyway.

28
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:56,710
♪ It's a long, long way to Ba Sing Se

29
00:01:56,793 --> 00:02:02,507
♪ But the girls in the city
They look so pretty ♪

30
00:02:02,924 --> 00:02:05,593
Come on, we're talking a gold piece here.

31
00:02:05,677 --> 00:02:06,761
Let's see some action.

32
00:02:08,096 --> 00:02:09,597
Dance.

33
00:02:09,723 --> 00:02:14,102
♪ They kiss so sweet
That you really have to meet

34
00:02:14,477 --> 00:02:18,606
♪ The girls from Ba Sing Se ♪

35
00:02:18,982 --> 00:02:22,027
( LAUGHING )

36
00:02:22,152 --> 00:02:25,155
Nothing like a fat man
dancing for his dinner.

37
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,614
Here you go.

38
00:02:29,534 --> 00:02:32,579
Such a kind man.

39
00:02:39,002 --> 00:02:40,503
( CHATTERS )

40
00:02:55,602 --> 00:02:58,855
Hey, you taking us down for a reason?

41
00:02:59,272 --> 00:03:01,608
Aang, why are we going down?

42
00:03:01,733 --> 00:03:02,859
What?

43
00:03:02,984 --> 00:03:04,194
I didn't even notice.

44
00:03:04,736 --> 00:03:06,863
SOKKA: Are you noticing now?

45
00:03:07,113 --> 00:03:08,281
Is something wrong?

46
00:03:08,531 --> 00:03:10,283
I know this is gonna sound weird,

47
00:03:10,408 --> 00:03:13,328
but I think the swamp is... calling to me.

48
00:03:13,411 --> 00:03:15,872
Is it telling you where we
can get something to eat?

49
00:03:15,955 --> 00:03:19,542
AANG: No, I, I think it wants us
to land there.

50
00:03:19,667 --> 00:03:20,835
No offense to the swamp,

51
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:23,505
but I don't see any land there to land on.

52
00:03:23,588 --> 00:03:24,589
I don't know.

53
00:03:24,672 --> 00:03:27,801
Bumi said to learn earthbending,
I would have to wait and listen.

54
00:03:27,926 --> 00:03:30,095
And now, I'm actually hearing the earth.

55
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:31,721
Do you want me to ignore it?

56
00:03:31,846 --> 00:03:32,889
( CHATTERS )

57
00:03:33,014 --> 00:03:34,641
- Yes.
- I don't know.

58
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,811
There's something ominous
about that place.

59
00:03:38,436 --> 00:03:39,938
( CHATTERS )

60
00:03:40,188 --> 00:03:41,314
( GRUMBLES )

61
00:03:41,398 --> 00:03:43,900
See? Even Appa and Momo
don't like it here.

62
00:03:44,109 --> 00:03:48,488
Okay, since everyone feels so
strongly about this, bye, swamp.

63
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,198
Yip yip!

64
00:03:51,991 --> 00:03:54,994
( RUMBLING )

65
00:03:55,495 --> 00:03:58,206
SOKKA: You better throw in an extra yip.
We gotta move.

66
00:04:08,675 --> 00:04:09,759
Ahh!

67
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:11,886
( YELLING )

68
00:04:25,859 --> 00:04:28,695
ALL: ( SCREAMING )

69
00:04:35,535 --> 00:04:36,703
( GROANS )

70
00:04:39,539 --> 00:04:41,040
Where's Appa and Momo?

71
00:04:47,505 --> 00:04:48,923
Appa!

72
00:04:49,048 --> 00:04:50,508
Momo!

73
00:04:54,137 --> 00:04:56,014
Sokka, you've got an elbow leech.

74
00:04:56,139 --> 00:04:57,432
Where, where?

75
00:04:57,557 --> 00:04:59,851
Where do you think?

76
00:04:59,976 --> 00:05:02,729
Why do things keep attaching to me?

77
00:05:04,439 --> 00:05:06,191
You couldn't find them?

78
00:05:06,316 --> 00:05:07,358
No...

79
00:05:07,484 --> 00:05:10,528
And the tornado, it just disappeared.

80
00:05:16,326 --> 00:05:18,411
-( GRUMBLING )
-( CHATTERS )

81
00:05:21,289 --> 00:05:22,540
( ROARS )

82
00:05:44,395 --> 00:05:46,814
( ROARS )

83
00:05:47,982 --> 00:05:49,234
We better speed things up.

84
00:05:51,069 --> 00:05:53,863
Maybe we should be a little
nicer to the swamp.

85
00:05:54,197 --> 00:05:55,615
Aang, these are just plants.

86
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:57,742
Do you want me to say please and thank you

87
00:05:57,825 --> 00:05:59,744
as I swing my machete back and forth?

88
00:05:59,869 --> 00:06:01,496
Maybe you should listen to Aang.

89
00:06:01,913 --> 00:06:05,458
Something about this place feels... alive.

90
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:08,419
I'm sure there are lots of things
that are alive here.

91
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:11,256
And if we don't want to wind
up getting eaten by them,

92
00:06:11,381 --> 00:06:13,841
we need to find Appa as fast as we can.

93
00:06:37,282 --> 00:06:38,575
( BLOWS WHISTLE )

94
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:39,742
( ROARS )

95
00:06:41,369 --> 00:06:42,495
( BLOWS WHISTLE )

96
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,664
( GURGLES )

97
00:06:47,166 --> 00:06:48,293
KATARA: Appa!

98
00:06:48,543 --> 00:06:50,128
Momo?

99
00:06:50,378 --> 00:06:53,172
There's no way they can hear us
and no way we can see them.

100
00:06:53,548 --> 00:06:55,550
We'll have to make camp for the night.

101
00:06:56,301 --> 00:06:58,720
-( INSECTS BUZZING )
- Ah, ugh!

102
00:06:59,679 --> 00:07:00,847
What was that?

103
00:07:01,472 --> 00:07:03,057
Nothing, just swamp gas.

104
00:07:03,141 --> 00:07:05,560
Look, there's nothing
supernatural going on here.

105
00:07:06,019 --> 00:07:07,103
ALL: Ugh...

106
00:07:07,228 --> 00:07:08,938
( HUMAN-LIKE SCREAMS )

107
00:07:09,063 --> 00:07:10,565
( SCREAMS )

108
00:07:11,065 --> 00:07:13,192
I think we should build a fire.

109
00:07:16,613 --> 00:07:18,072
Sokka, the longer we're here,

110
00:07:18,156 --> 00:07:20,325
the more I think you
shouldn't be doing that.

111
00:07:20,617 --> 00:07:21,743
No, I asked the swamp.

112
00:07:21,826 --> 00:07:24,370
It said this was fine. Right, swamp?

113
00:07:24,621 --> 00:07:26,664
( SQUEAKILY ) No problem, Sokka.

114
00:07:32,545 --> 00:07:35,632
Does anyone else get the feeling
that we're being watched?

115
00:07:35,923 --> 00:07:38,885
Please, we're all alone out here.

116
00:07:39,385 --> 00:07:41,054
( GRUNTING )

117
00:07:44,849 --> 00:07:47,352
Except for them.

118
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,520
Right, except for them.

119
00:07:50,438 --> 00:07:53,232
( FROGS CROAKING )

120
00:07:53,691 --> 00:07:59,030
( INDISTINCT ANIMAL NOISES )

121
00:08:03,368 --> 00:08:06,579
( ROARS )

122
00:08:07,288 --> 00:08:09,749
( ANIMAL NOISES STOP )

123
00:08:36,275 --> 00:08:37,485
ALL: ( YELLING )

124
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:38,611
Hagh!

125
00:08:38,736 --> 00:08:39,737
Ahh!

126
00:08:39,821 --> 00:08:41,072
Ahh!

127
00:08:55,128 --> 00:08:56,963
( GRUNTING )

128
00:09:07,014 --> 00:09:08,641
Ugh.

129
00:09:12,437 --> 00:09:13,479
Ahh!

130
00:09:13,730 --> 00:09:14,856
Ugh...

131
00:09:20,737 --> 00:09:22,739
Guys?

132
00:09:27,618 --> 00:09:30,204
What'd you reckon
make a track like that, Tho?

133
00:09:30,413 --> 00:09:31,789
Don't know, Due.

134
00:09:31,873 --> 00:09:35,918
Something with six legs,
pretty big 'uns, too.

135
00:09:36,544 --> 00:09:38,504
DUE: Leaves a nice, wide trail to follow.

136
00:09:38,963 --> 00:09:41,007
You know what's at the end of that trail?

137
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:44,093
Dinner.

138
00:09:55,188 --> 00:09:57,231
( ROARS )

139
00:10:03,029 --> 00:10:04,071
( GROWLS )

140
00:10:04,489 --> 00:10:05,698
( HISSING )

141
00:10:08,659 --> 00:10:10,244
( GRUMBLES )

142
00:10:16,793 --> 00:10:18,085
KATARA: Aang?

143
00:10:18,544 --> 00:10:20,254
Sokka?

144
00:10:23,049 --> 00:10:24,091
Hello?

145
00:10:24,175 --> 00:10:25,843
Hello.

146
00:10:25,927 --> 00:10:27,470
Can you help me?

147
00:10:29,096 --> 00:10:30,807
Mom?

148
00:10:30,890 --> 00:10:32,308
Mom!

149
00:10:35,686 --> 00:10:37,480
I can't believe...

150
00:10:37,897 --> 00:10:40,024
( GASPS )

151
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:42,944
( SOBBING )

152
00:10:47,824 --> 00:10:49,450
Aang!

153
00:10:49,909 --> 00:10:53,204
Stupid swamp. Dumb, ugly vines.

154
00:10:53,704 --> 00:10:55,331
Katara!

155
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:57,917
You think you're so tough, huh?

156
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,335
( GRUNTING )

157
00:10:59,418 --> 00:11:00,628
Ah!

158
00:11:04,924 --> 00:11:07,218
Hello?

159
00:11:10,721 --> 00:11:12,181
Yue?

160
00:11:12,431 --> 00:11:14,600
This is just a trick of the light...

161
00:11:14,809 --> 00:11:16,018
Swamp gas.

162
00:11:16,102 --> 00:11:18,229
I hit my head running away last night.

163
00:11:18,437 --> 00:11:20,481
I'm going crazy.

164
00:11:22,817 --> 00:11:25,444
( ECHOING ) You didn't protect me.
You didn't protect me.

165
00:11:27,947 --> 00:11:29,282
( SIGHS )

166
00:11:29,365 --> 00:11:30,700
Ah!

167
00:11:38,457 --> 00:11:41,294
Katara!

168
00:11:41,836 --> 00:11:43,212
Appa!

169
00:11:44,505 --> 00:11:45,548
Hello?

170
00:11:45,673 --> 00:11:47,300
Who are you?

171
00:11:47,425 --> 00:11:48,801
( LAUGHING )

172
00:11:48,926 --> 00:11:50,011
AANG: Hey!

173
00:11:50,136 --> 00:11:51,387
Come back.

174
00:11:53,514 --> 00:11:54,765
( LAUGHING )

175
00:11:58,936 --> 00:12:00,605
( GIGGLES )

176
00:12:07,236 --> 00:12:09,322
( LAUGHS )

177
00:12:25,922 --> 00:12:27,590
Lookee there, Tho.

178
00:12:27,673 --> 00:12:30,176
Is that a little hairy
fella riding that thing?

179
00:12:30,384 --> 00:12:32,595
No, that's what they call a "Iemu."

180
00:12:32,887 --> 00:12:36,349
Saw one at a traveling show once.
Real smart, they say.

181
00:12:36,432 --> 00:12:38,559
Bet he tastes a lot like possum-chicken.

182
00:12:38,643 --> 00:12:41,270
You think everything tastes
like possum-chicken.

183
00:12:41,479 --> 00:12:44,732
Come on, now, fellas,
just a little closer.

184
00:12:44,815 --> 00:12:46,400
Nice and easy.

185
00:12:46,609 --> 00:12:47,944
Nothin' to worry about.

186
00:12:48,027 --> 00:12:49,487
We just fixin' to eat ya.

187
00:12:50,029 --> 00:12:51,364
( GROWLS )

188
00:12:51,489 --> 00:12:52,865
What'd ya say that fer?

189
00:12:52,949 --> 00:12:54,116
Well, we are.

190
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,993
But you don't have to tell them that.

191
00:12:56,077 --> 00:12:57,870
How'd I know they'd understand me?

192
00:12:57,954 --> 00:12:59,997
Come on.

193
00:13:19,392 --> 00:13:21,352
( LAUGHING )

194
00:13:26,941 --> 00:13:28,901
Who are you?

195
00:13:33,155 --> 00:13:34,824
BOTH: Ahh!

196
00:13:35,574 --> 00:13:36,659
Ugh.

197
00:13:36,742 --> 00:13:37,827
ALL: ( GROANING )

198
00:13:38,703 --> 00:13:40,579
What do you guys think you're doing?

199
00:13:40,663 --> 00:13:42,873
I've been looking all over for you.

200
00:13:42,957 --> 00:13:45,251
Well, I've been wandering
around looking for you.

201
00:13:45,459 --> 00:13:47,378
I was chasing some girl.

202
00:13:47,586 --> 00:13:49,463
- What girl?
- I don't know.

203
00:13:50,006 --> 00:13:52,717
I heard laughing, and I saw
some girl in a fancy dress.

204
00:13:52,967 --> 00:13:54,760
Well, there must be a tea party here,

205
00:13:54,844 --> 00:13:57,138
and we just didn't get our invitations.

206
00:13:57,972 --> 00:13:59,807
I thought I saw Mom.

207
00:14:02,143 --> 00:14:04,103
Look, we were all just scared and hungry,

208
00:14:04,186 --> 00:14:06,105
and our minds were playing tricks on us.

209
00:14:06,188 --> 00:14:08,024
That's why we all saw things out here.

210
00:14:08,149 --> 00:14:09,859
You saw something, too?

211
00:14:09,942 --> 00:14:11,110
I thought I saw Yue.

212
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,903
But that doesn't prove anything.

213
00:14:13,279 --> 00:14:15,281
Look, I think about her all the time.

214
00:14:15,531 --> 00:14:17,616
And you saw Mom, someone you miss a lot.

215
00:14:17,950 --> 00:14:19,493
What about me?

216
00:14:19,577 --> 00:14:21,162
I didn't know the girl I saw.

217
00:14:21,454 --> 00:14:23,831
And all our visions led us right here.

218
00:14:24,165 --> 00:14:27,376
Okay, so where's here,
the middle of the swamp?

219
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,919
Yeah...

220
00:14:29,003 --> 00:14:31,297
The center.

221
00:14:32,965 --> 00:14:34,425
It's the heart of the swamp.

222
00:14:34,508 --> 00:14:35,843
It's been calling us here.

223
00:14:36,093 --> 00:14:37,386
I knew it.

224
00:14:37,678 --> 00:14:40,806
It's just a tree. It can't call anyone.

225
00:14:41,057 --> 00:14:43,350
For the last time,
there's nothing after us,

226
00:14:43,434 --> 00:14:46,437
and there's nothing
magical happening here.

227
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:49,565
ALL: ( SCREAMING )

228
00:15:12,088 --> 00:15:14,256
Ahh!

229
00:15:14,882 --> 00:15:16,008
( GRUNTING )

230
00:15:26,143 --> 00:15:27,311
( GRUNTS )

231
00:15:38,239 --> 00:15:40,491
Ah!

232
00:15:41,117 --> 00:15:42,535
Ugh!

233
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:50,584
KATARA: ( GROANS )

234
00:15:51,335 --> 00:15:53,337
- Ahh!
- Unh!

235
00:16:02,972 --> 00:16:04,098
( GROWLING )

236
00:16:12,398 --> 00:16:14,191
Ah!

237
00:16:15,985 --> 00:16:18,070
( GRUNTING )

238
00:16:18,904 --> 00:16:21,907
Now, what would a "Iemu" need a shirt fer?

239
00:16:22,032 --> 00:16:23,075
Ahh!

240
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,202
Ugh!

241
00:16:35,296 --> 00:16:37,298
( GROWLING )

242
00:16:44,263 --> 00:16:45,931
( GRUNTING )

243
00:17:03,991 --> 00:17:05,951
BOTH: Ugh!

244
00:17:12,625 --> 00:17:13,626
Ah!

245
00:17:15,961 --> 00:17:17,004
Ugh.

246
00:17:17,713 --> 00:17:19,798
( SCREAMING )

247
00:17:19,882 --> 00:17:20,966
Ugh!

248
00:17:35,439 --> 00:17:38,359
There's someone in there!
He's bending the vines.

249
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,778
( GRUNTS )

250
00:17:46,033 --> 00:17:47,117
Ah!

251
00:17:52,414 --> 00:17:55,000
Why did you call me here
if you just wanted to kill us?

252
00:17:55,542 --> 00:17:57,127
Wait!

253
00:17:57,211 --> 00:17:59,255
I didn't call you here.

254
00:18:01,215 --> 00:18:03,926
We were flying over, and I heard
something calling to me,

255
00:18:04,009 --> 00:18:05,010
telling me to land.

256
00:18:05,177 --> 00:18:06,512
He's the Avatar.

257
00:18:06,595 --> 00:18:08,472
Stuff like that happens to us a lot.

258
00:18:08,555 --> 00:18:10,182
The Avatar?

259
00:18:10,266 --> 00:18:11,517
Come with me.

260
00:18:14,436 --> 00:18:16,313
KATARA: So who are you, then?

261
00:18:16,939 --> 00:18:19,942
I protect the swamp from
folks that want to hurt it,

262
00:18:20,025 --> 00:18:22,027
like this fellow with his big knife.

263
00:18:22,152 --> 00:18:23,362
See?

264
00:18:23,487 --> 00:18:25,364
Completely reasonable. Not a monster,

265
00:18:25,447 --> 00:18:27,283
just a regular guy defending his home.

266
00:18:27,408 --> 00:18:29,618
Nothing mystical about it.

267
00:18:30,577 --> 00:18:33,580
MAN: Oh, the swamp is a mystical place,
all right.

268
00:18:33,706 --> 00:18:34,832
It's sacred.

269
00:18:35,457 --> 00:18:39,586
I reached enlightenment right here,
under the banyan grove tree.

270
00:18:39,670 --> 00:18:42,756
I heard it calling me, just like you did.

271
00:18:43,632 --> 00:18:46,593
Sure you did. It seems real chatty.

272
00:18:47,970 --> 00:18:51,265
See, this whole swamp
is actually just one tree

273
00:18:51,390 --> 00:18:53,225
spread out over miles.

274
00:18:53,309 --> 00:18:56,353
Branches spread and sink and take root

275
00:18:56,437 --> 00:18:58,856
and then spread some more...

276
00:18:58,939 --> 00:19:01,567
One big, living organism,

277
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:04,820
just like the entire world.

278
00:19:06,030 --> 00:19:10,200
I get how the tree is one big thing,
but the whole world?

279
00:19:10,284 --> 00:19:11,285
Sure.

280
00:19:11,493 --> 00:19:13,162
You think you're any different

281
00:19:13,245 --> 00:19:16,081
from me or your friends or this tree?

282
00:19:16,498 --> 00:19:18,334
If you listen hard enough,

283
00:19:18,417 --> 00:19:21,837
you can hear every living thing
breathing together.

284
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:24,923
You can feel everything growing.

285
00:19:25,549 --> 00:19:29,345
We are all living together,
even if most folks don't act like it.

286
00:19:29,803 --> 00:19:32,014
We all have the same roots,

287
00:19:32,139 --> 00:19:35,601
and we are all branches of the same tree.

288
00:19:35,851 --> 00:19:37,728
KATARA: But what did our visions mean?

289
00:19:37,811 --> 00:19:41,440
In the swamp, we see visions
of people we've lost,

290
00:19:41,648 --> 00:19:45,361
people we loved, folks we think are gone.

291
00:19:45,486 --> 00:19:50,324
But the swamp tells us they're not.
We're still connected to 'em.

292
00:19:50,449 --> 00:19:54,244
Time is an illusion, and so is death.

293
00:19:54,536 --> 00:19:56,330
But what about my vision?

294
00:19:56,413 --> 00:19:57,915
It was someone I had never met.

295
00:19:58,332 --> 00:20:00,542
You're the Avatar. You tell me.

296
00:20:01,418 --> 00:20:04,046
Time is an illusion...

297
00:20:04,838 --> 00:20:08,133
So, it's someone I will meet.

298
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:13,263
Sorry to interrupt the lesson,
but we still need to find Appa and Momo.

299
00:20:13,555 --> 00:20:15,599
I think I know how to find them.

300
00:20:15,974 --> 00:20:18,435
Everything is connected.

301
00:20:37,121 --> 00:20:38,914
Come on, we've gotta hurry!

302
00:20:39,415 --> 00:20:42,626
♪ Set my lines by the riverbed

303
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:46,213
♪ Caught ten fish, and I killed 'em dead

304
00:20:46,338 --> 00:20:49,174
♪ Cut 'em and gut 'em
And I toss the heads

305
00:20:49,258 --> 00:20:52,886
♪ In the water
To keep them cat-gators fed ♪

306
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:57,182
( SCREAMING )

307
00:20:58,434 --> 00:20:59,768
Appa!

308
00:21:00,644 --> 00:21:02,020
Oh!

309
00:21:02,104 --> 00:21:03,814
We're under attack!

310
00:21:07,734 --> 00:21:09,987
Hey, you guys are waterbenders.

311
00:21:10,571 --> 00:21:11,697
You, too?

312
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:13,740
That means we're kin.

313
00:21:19,121 --> 00:21:21,081
Hey, Huu. How you been?

314
00:21:21,457 --> 00:21:26,462
You know, scared some folks,
swung some vines... The usual.

315
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,172
Huu?

316
00:21:28,255 --> 00:21:31,758
( TWANGY MUSIC PLAYING )

317
00:21:31,967 --> 00:21:33,760
How you like that possum-chicken?

318
00:21:33,844 --> 00:21:35,804
Tastes just like arctic hen.

319
00:21:36,054 --> 00:21:38,474
So why were you guys
so interested in eating Appa?

320
00:21:38,557 --> 00:21:41,143
You've got plenty of those
big things wandering around.

321
00:21:41,351 --> 00:21:43,187
You want me to eat ol' Slim?

322
00:21:43,437 --> 00:21:46,064
He's like a member of the family.

323
00:21:46,482 --> 00:21:47,816
Nice Slim.

324
00:21:47,941 --> 00:21:49,693
-( GROWLS )
- Ah!

325
00:21:50,068 --> 00:21:52,696
( LAUGHING ) Oh, he don't eat no bugs.

326
00:21:52,779 --> 00:21:54,198
That's people food.

327
00:21:54,531 --> 00:21:56,200
Where'd you say you was from?

328
00:21:56,283 --> 00:21:57,451
The South Pole.

329
00:21:57,618 --> 00:22:00,120
Didn't know there was
waterbenders anywhere but here.

330
00:22:00,204 --> 00:22:02,206
They got a nice swamp there, do they?

331
00:22:02,289 --> 00:22:04,791
No, it's all ice and snow.

332
00:22:05,292 --> 00:22:07,669
Hmm, no wonder you left.

333
00:22:07,794 --> 00:22:09,296
Well, I hope you realize now

334
00:22:09,379 --> 00:22:11,924
that nothing strange was going on here.

335
00:22:12,007 --> 00:22:14,301
Just a bunch of greasy people
living in a swamp.

336
00:22:14,468 --> 00:22:16,136
What about the visions?

337
00:22:16,261 --> 00:22:18,388
I told you, we were hungry.

338
00:22:18,472 --> 00:22:20,933
I'm eating a giant bug.

339
00:22:22,100 --> 00:22:23,977
Mmm-ugh.

340
00:22:24,061 --> 00:22:27,105
But what about when the tree showed me
where Appa and Momo were?

341
00:22:27,314 --> 00:22:29,274
That's Avatar stuff, that doesn't count.

342
00:22:29,399 --> 00:22:31,026
The only thing I can't figure out

343
00:22:31,109 --> 00:22:33,362
is how you made the tornado
that sucked us down.

344
00:22:33,570 --> 00:22:35,822
I can't do anything like that.

345
00:22:35,906 --> 00:22:38,450
I just bend the water in the plants.

346
00:22:39,326 --> 00:22:41,161
Well, no accounting for weather.

347
00:22:41,453 --> 00:22:44,831
Still, there's absolutely
nothing mysterious about the swamp.

348
00:22:49,044 --> 00:22:50,212
( SCREAMS )

349
00:22:50,337 --> 00:22:51,380
( THWACKS )

350
00:22:59,721 --> 00:23:01,473
Who's there?

351
00:23:04,643 --> 00:23:05,852
Whoa!

352
00:23:05,936 --> 00:23:06,979
Ugh...

353
00:23:20,158 --> 00:23:22,160
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
